<Base title="About" description="About Card Night, an independent local guide to Pokémon card nights in Austin, TX.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About Card Night</h1>
    <p class="lede">Card Night is an independent guide for Austin-area parents whose kids caught the Pokémon card bug.</p>
    <p>Finding a friendly place to play is harder than it should be. Store schedules are spread across Facebook pages, event locators, and flyers, and not every event suits a nervous 8-year-old. We gather the basics in one place: where, when, how much, and whether it works for kids.</p>
    <h2>How we list places</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We only list real stores and events we found on the store's own site, the organizer's page, or the official event locators.</li>
      <li>We never invent events, prices, or reviews. If we couldn't confirm a schedule, the listing says so.</li>
      <li>Each listing links to its source so you can double-check.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How we'll keep the lights on</h2>
    <p>Later we may add clearly labeled sponsored spots for local shops and shows, and affiliate links for supplies like sleeves and binders. Paid placements will always be labeled and won't change what we say.</p>
    <p>Card Night is fan-made and not affiliated with Nintendo, The Pokémon Company, Creatures, or Game Freak.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
